-- the review of w_agg_subsumption (2026-09-30) found five proofs wanting:
-- eval_rust's (a monotone consumer an improvement reached back through a
-- plain relation was refused, where the min lattice answers), ticks' (a
-- conclusion staged @next from a fact withdrawn later in the tick stayed
-- staged; the same held for a lattice's hole, so order_lattice's ticks proof
-- was wanting too), holes' (a value whose only comparison, with itself,
-- faults was proven by no world), why's (whynot read a faulting or unknown
-- comparison as no) and safety's (the door read a dominance body in no
-- order). Each is closed again only by the strengthened agg_sub_eval,
-- agg_sub_ticks, agg_lattice_ticks, agg_sub_holes, agg_sub_why and
-- agg_sub_safety, red under `dominance_history_unfounded`,
-- `staged_keeps_withdrawn`, `dominance_self_fault_ignored`,
-- `dominance_whynot_unasked` and `dominance_body_unordered`.
