-- PER-KEY PRECISION (w_agg_precise_holes, docs/aggregates.md, "Precise
-- holes, as built"). A grouped body aggregate or a counting tag whose inner
-- body could read an unknown held the whole correlation a hole, every key of
-- the tag withdrawn (f_a_counting_tag_fault_holes_every_key_of_the_tag). The
-- holes and shrug cells of every kind that reads a plain unknown through a
-- body aggregate are REOPENED here, their claims moved from w_agg_shrug,
-- w_agg_tags and the holes sweep, and closed again only by the worlds that
-- hold each group to what every completion of the unknowns gives it.
work(w_agg_precise_holes, "per-key precision: what a hole left out reaches exactly the groups of a grouped body aggregate (count, sum, min, max, or, and, median, quantile, rank) and the keys of a counting tag whose value it could change, each a hole on its own cell, decided under every completion where it cannot (a projection held, a value no possible improves on, a sum it does not move, an order statistic neither extreme moves); a group only an unknown could make a cell of its own; a possible whose group is not known the correlation's hole beside the groups sealed; in both engines, with a completions oracle").
work_state(w_agg_precise_holes, done).
work_needs(w_agg_precise_holes, w_agg_shrug).
work_needs(w_agg_precise_holes, w_agg_tags).
